==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Neneko was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[The Divas (Removed Combo)|The Divas]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]], Neneko, [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]], [[Cat Base Mini (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Base Mini]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] could only be unlocked when "Limited Edition" was part of the current pool.
*Unlike Moneko and Koneko, Neneko's name in her Evolved Form is capitalized. Moneko's capitalization was removed in [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], and Koneko's name was never capitalized.
*The Cat that carries her in her Normal Form is covered by a milk crate, while on [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] it's a beer crate.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Neneko and Moneko share the same death soul, but in the mobile versions, Neneko just uses the default one.
*Ironically, Neneko is the only variant of herself to not have a [[True Form]].
*Not counting [[:Category:Collaboration Event Cats|Collaboration Cats]], Neneko is the oldest existing Super Rare Cat without a True Form.
*The ''neko'' in Moneko's, Neneko's and [[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Koneko]]'s names means ''cat'', likely meant to represent the fact that they are ''[[wikipedia:Catgirl|Nekomimi]]'', or people with the ears and tail of a cat.

